==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{attention|la}} {{term|serratus||saw shaped|lang=la}}, from {{term|serra||saw|lang=la}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-|-}}

# [[saw]]-like.
#: ''That knife has a '''serrated''' blade.''
# Having a row of [[sharp]] or [[tooth]]-like [[projection]]s.
#: ''Maple leaves have '''serrated''' edges.''

